1
00:00:00,343 --> 00:00:01,343
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,343 --> 00:00:02,343
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,343 --> 00:00:03,343
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:08,543 --> 00:00:10,276
[The Salvation Army Red Kettle]

5
00:00:15,815 --> 00:00:18,023
Merry Christmas!

6
00:00:24,583 --> 00:00:27,271
Merry Christmas!

7
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:42,959
What is it?

8
00:01:14,576 --> 00:01:16,243
Ji Ah, I got you a present.

9
00:01:16,243 --> 00:01:19,276
Wow! A teddy bear!

10
00:01:19,276 --> 00:01:21,910
Thank you so much, Daddy!

11
00:01:58,276 --> 00:02:02,343
It's been seven years
since I last saw your face.

12
00:02:02,343 --> 00:02:07,510
I've missed you so much all that time.

13
00:02:13,351 --> 00:02:19,610
More than anything,
I'm sorry for leaving you all alone.

14
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:25,310
I've blamed myself every single day.

15
00:02:27,010 --> 00:02:28,776
That day...

16
00:02:30,776 --> 00:02:33,476
I shouldn't have done that that day.

17
00:02:43,076 --> 00:02:47,410
I think something got into it.
I'll get you another one.

18
00:03:00,376 --> 00:03:02,543
You turned out so well, my daughter.

19
00:03:02,543 --> 00:03:07,810
Now that I see you,
you look just like your late mom.

20
00:03:10,276 --> 00:03:12,943
For seven years in prison,

21
00:03:12,943 --> 00:03:16,810
I stared at the ceiling every night,
filled with regret.

22
00:03:18,043 --> 00:03:19,810
That day...

23
00:03:25,076 --> 00:03:28,410
I should've killed you too.

24
00:03:29,110 --> 00:03:31,176
- Let go!
- You ungrateful brat!

25
00:03:31,176 --> 00:03:33,310
After everything I did for you,
you reported your own dad?

26
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:37,510
Do you have any idea how long
I've been waiting for this day?

27
00:03:40,276 --> 00:03:42,143
You little...

28
00:03:44,647 --> 00:03:46,187
You brat.

29
00:03:47,376 --> 00:03:49,343
Where do you think you're going?

30
00:03:51,076 --> 00:03:54,343
I'll finish what I should've done back then.

31
00:03:56,391 --> 00:03:58,151
You little brat.

32
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:03,143
Get over here. Get over here!

33
00:04:12,510 --> 00:04:14,443
Stay still, you punk.

34
00:04:14,443 --> 00:04:16,076
The more you struggle,
the harder it'll be on you.

35
00:04:16,076 --> 00:04:17,967
Relax...

36
00:04:18,943 --> 00:04:22,843
It's time for you to go meet your mom too.

37
00:05:11,076 --> 00:05:13,943
[Machine Wash]

38
00:05:47,455 --> 00:05:48,455
[Merry Christmas]

39
00:05:48,455 --> 00:05:51,376
Do you want a Christmas present?

40
00:05:52,576 --> 00:05:54,810
Then no crying.

41
00:05:56,410 --> 00:05:58,776
You have to be good.

42
00:05:59,443 --> 00:06:03,335
I heard that Santa is very clear
about right and wrong.

43
00:06:03,335 --> 00:06:04,976
Miss, who are you?

44
00:06:04,976 --> 00:06:09,543
Leave the living room window
slightly open when you get home.

45
00:06:09,543 --> 00:06:11,643
And leave the lights on.

46
00:06:18,376 --> 00:06:20,043
See you again.

47
00:07:09,210 --> 00:07:14,990
[15 Years Later, Present Day]

48
00:07:30,210 --> 00:07:33,010
Mommy, wake up!

49
00:07:33,010 --> 00:07:34,843
Yul, you're awake?

50
00:07:34,843 --> 00:07:36,443
Daddy, wake up too!

51
00:07:36,443 --> 00:07:38,276
Five more minutes, just five...

52
00:07:38,276 --> 00:07:42,276
No, you have to go to work!

53
00:07:43,010 --> 00:07:46,643
Yul really takes after you,
no doubt about it.

54
00:07:46,643 --> 00:07:49,576
Jeez, she's listening.

55
00:07:49,576 --> 00:07:54,076
My Yul, you're so smart
because you take after your daddy.

56
00:07:54,076 --> 00:07:55,976
Are you awake?

57
00:07:55,976 --> 00:07:57,776
Really?

58
00:07:57,776 --> 00:07:59,910
Are you so smart
because you take after me, Yul?

59
00:07:59,910 --> 00:08:01,010
Yul, come here!

60
00:08:01,010 --> 00:08:03,510
Daddy, get up already.

61
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:07,443
Oh, my little precious. Come here.

62
00:08:07,443 --> 00:08:09,343
Yul, did you sleep well?

63
00:08:10,076 --> 00:08:12,103
I think we put her to bed too early.

64
00:08:12,103 --> 00:08:16,243
Well, who was it that insisted
on putting her to bed so early?

65
00:08:16,243 --> 00:08:18,110
Was that me?

66
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:21,976
Then our big precious too...

67
00:08:21,976 --> 00:08:24,110
I need to go potty.

68
00:08:24,110 --> 00:08:26,376
- Potty...
- Let's go potty.

69
00:08:26,376 --> 00:08:29,576
Come on. Let's go potty.

70
00:08:29,576 --> 00:08:32,543
Let's go! Let's go potty.

71
00:08:37,110 --> 00:08:40,110
[Episode 1]

72
00:08:54,276 --> 00:08:57,876
The monster's coming after you!
I'll catch you!

73
00:08:57,876 --> 00:09:03,303
Let's go! Yul, let's go! Come on!

74
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:12,103
[Kwon Yul, Dad, Mom]

75
00:09:36,276 --> 00:09:37,710
All done! Let's go!

76
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:39,443
Daddy! The swings!

77
00:09:39,443 --> 00:09:41,876
The swings!

78
00:09:46,215 --> 00:09:47,815
Well, it's good, right?

79
00:09:48,476 --> 00:09:51,076
Four-year-olds can eat on their own, right?

80
00:09:51,076 --> 00:09:52,143
Yeah.

81
00:09:52,143 --> 00:09:55,576
Go ahead, Yul. Try eating by yourself.

82
00:09:55,576 --> 00:09:58,343
Time for an important decision.

83
00:09:58,343 --> 00:10:02,776
The selfish new look, bought with money
stashed away from my wife.

84
00:10:02,776 --> 00:10:06,510
Or the rebellious night out, lying about
working late and heading to the club.

85
00:10:06,510 --> 00:10:08,143
Which one?

86
00:10:09,276 --> 00:10:11,559
The rebel look today?

87
00:10:11,559 --> 00:10:14,310
Oh, my! Really?

88
00:10:14,310 --> 00:10:17,510
Wow, my wife is so generous.

89
00:10:19,543 --> 00:10:22,076
When was the last time I went clubbing?

90
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:25,310
Yul, did you eat it all by yourself?

91
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:27,676
Awesome! You can eat all by yourself now!

92
00:10:27,676 --> 00:10:31,210
Daddy! Yul finished all her food.

93
00:10:31,210 --> 00:10:34,076
Really? You ate it all by yourself?

94
00:10:35,376 --> 00:10:37,310
That's amazing, my girl!

95
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:39,243
What time is it? Oh, time to get dressed.

96
00:10:39,243 --> 00:10:40,443
Let's go!

97
00:10:40,443 --> 00:10:43,343
Let's go, let's go! Let's get you changed.

98
00:10:43,343 --> 00:10:46,043
Honey, her P.E. uniform is over there.

99
00:10:46,043 --> 00:10:47,343
Yul, do you have P.E. today?

100
00:10:47,343 --> 00:10:48,576
- Yeah.
- That's nice.

101
00:10:48,576 --> 00:10:49,876
- What time is it?
- Okay, then,

102
00:10:49,876 --> 00:10:52,176
stand on one foot for five seconds.

103
00:10:52,176 --> 00:10:53,443
Start!

104
00:10:53,443 --> 00:10:55,043
One, two, three, four, five!

105
00:10:55,810 --> 00:10:57,543
Success!

106
00:10:57,543 --> 00:11:00,210
- Success!
- Success!

107
00:11:00,210 --> 00:11:03,143
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three!

108
00:11:03,143 --> 00:11:06,010
- One, two, three!
- One more time. One, two, three!

109
00:11:06,010 --> 00:11:08,576
Have fun with your friends. See you tonight!

110
00:11:08,576 --> 00:11:10,887
- Okay! Bye-bye!
- Bye-bye!

111
00:11:10,887 --> 00:11:12,210
Here.

112
00:11:14,576 --> 00:11:15,776
What?

113
00:11:15,776 --> 00:11:20,263
I feel like I had an important reason
to get off work early today.

114
00:11:20,263 --> 00:11:22,176
What was it?

115
00:11:25,676 --> 00:11:28,076
Seriously, what was it?

116
00:11:28,076 --> 00:11:30,276
Well, what could it be?

117
00:11:32,076 --> 00:11:33,776
You're not falling for it, huh?

118
00:11:35,310 --> 00:11:40,176
I'll be home early today.
For my honey's big day tomorrow.

119
00:11:40,176 --> 00:11:42,410
Oh, stop it.

120
00:11:43,476 --> 00:11:47,210
But if you'd forgotten,
you would've been in big trouble.

121
00:11:48,043 --> 00:11:49,910
I really hope not.

122
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:51,710
Right.

123
00:11:52,710 --> 00:11:57,743
Ms. Yoo Bo Na, have a great day today.
And I'll see you this evening.

124
00:11:57,743 --> 00:11:59,376
Alright.

125
00:12:00,110 --> 00:12:01,543
What about what we didn't do earlier?

126
00:12:01,543 --> 00:12:03,143
Now!

127
00:12:03,143 --> 00:12:04,643
I'll get going. Bye-bye.

128
00:12:04,643 --> 00:12:06,143
- Bye!
- Me too!

129
00:12:06,143 --> 00:12:07,176
A kiss for Yul too!

130
00:12:07,176 --> 00:12:09,410
A kiss for Yul too! Bye!

131
00:12:09,410 --> 00:12:10,410
Bye-bye!

132
00:12:10,410 --> 00:12:11,576
- See you later.
- Have a good day!

133
00:12:11,576 --> 00:12:14,176
- I'll get going.
- Yul, I'm closing the door.

134
00:12:17,510 --> 00:12:19,876
<i>♪ Baby shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪</i>

135
00:12:19,876 --> 00:12:22,727
<i>♪ Yul shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪</i>

136
00:12:22,727 --> 00:12:25,243
<i>♪ Mommy shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪</i>

137
00:12:25,243 --> 00:12:27,610
<i>♪ Daddy shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪</i>

138
00:12:27,610 --> 00:12:29,210
<i>♪ Grandma ♪</i>

139
00:12:31,610 --> 00:12:33,876
<i>♪ Doo, doo, doo, doo ♪</i>

140
00:12:47,343 --> 00:12:49,410
Yul, shall we sing the song again?

141
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:53,610
<i>♪ Daddy shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪</i>

142
00:12:53,610 --> 00:12:57,476
Yes, yes. Don't run! Be careful, careful!

143
00:12:58,243 --> 00:12:59,843
- Goodbye!
- Yeah, yeah.

144
00:12:59,843 --> 00:13:00,976
Take care.

145
00:13:00,976 --> 00:13:03,143
Seo Jun!

146
00:13:03,810 --> 00:13:04,810
Up you go.

147
00:13:04,810 --> 00:13:06,110
Please take good care of him today.

148
00:13:06,110 --> 00:13:07,643
Be sure to listen to your teacher, okay?

149
00:13:07,643 --> 00:13:09,710
- I'll be off.
- Okay, have a good day, Ma'am.

150
00:13:09,710 --> 00:13:11,510
- Hello!
- Hello!

151
00:13:12,410 --> 00:13:13,743
Hello.

152
00:13:13,743 --> 00:13:15,976
Hello!

153
00:13:15,976 --> 00:13:18,076
- Hello.
- Hello!

154
00:13:18,076 --> 00:13:21,743
She always looks so relaxed. It's nice.

155
00:13:21,743 --> 00:13:22,776
- Yul, you're here!
- Hello.

156
00:13:22,776 --> 00:13:25,276
Miss, I ate breakfast all by myself today.

157
00:13:25,276 --> 00:13:28,810
Oh, really? You did a great job.

158
00:13:28,810 --> 00:13:30,476
Yul, say hello to your teacher first.

159
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:33,910
- Give her a nice big bow.
- Good morning.

160
00:13:33,910 --> 00:13:35,543
Please take good care of her today too.

161
00:13:35,543 --> 00:13:38,476
Don't worry. Yul seems to have adjusted now.

162
00:13:38,476 --> 00:13:41,576
Totally different from the beginning,
she's playing well and doing great.

163
00:13:41,576 --> 00:13:43,976
That's thanks to you. Thank you.

164
00:13:43,976 --> 00:13:45,976
Yul, shall we say goodbye to Mommy today?

165
00:13:45,976 --> 00:13:47,843
Okay. My Yul.

166
00:13:47,843 --> 00:13:49,676
- Today, too, with friends,
- Today, too, with friends,

167
00:13:49,676 --> 00:13:51,576
- get along well!
- get along well!

168
00:13:51,576 --> 00:13:53,176
- Have a nice day!
- Yul, let's go.

169
00:13:53,176 --> 00:13:54,410
Have a good day, Ma'am. See you later.

170
00:13:54,410 --> 00:13:57,676
- Okay.
- Yul's mom!

171
00:13:57,676 --> 00:14:00,443
How about a morning coffee for a change?

172
00:14:00,443 --> 00:14:02,076
That sounds great.

173
00:14:03,310 --> 00:14:07,743
Oh, Ye Geon's mom,
did you not sleep well last night?

174
00:14:07,743 --> 00:14:10,343
My kid dozed off poorly
in the early evening, woke up,

175
00:14:10,343 --> 00:14:12,776
and then couldn't fall back asleep
until late at night.

176
00:14:12,776 --> 00:14:14,643
- Oh, dear, really?
- See?

177
00:14:14,643 --> 00:14:16,343
I told you, right?

178
00:14:16,343 --> 00:14:19,376
That's why you need to
stick to a daily routine.

179
00:14:19,376 --> 00:14:22,076
Otherwise, you'll end up twice as exhausted.

180
00:14:22,076 --> 00:14:28,527
Look at me. No matter how tired I am,
I never let my kid nap during the day.

181
00:14:29,143 --> 00:14:31,210
Right, naps...

182
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:34,510
By the way, isn't Seo Jun's mom amazing?

183
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:38,543
I saw earlier that she even seemed
to forget that today was P.E. day.

184
00:14:38,543 --> 00:14:42,743
I don't know how she manages
to work while raising a child.

185
00:14:44,743 --> 00:14:47,910
I'll... I'll go get it. You stay here.

186
00:14:49,943 --> 00:14:53,443
How can you say that
after seeing that poor child earlier?

187
00:14:56,510 --> 00:15:00,876
If you can't do both properly,
you should just focus on one thing.

188
00:15:00,876 --> 00:15:02,010
Oh, dear.

189
00:15:02,010 --> 00:15:04,943
I just feel sorry for her.

190
00:15:05,823 --> 00:15:06,823
Oh, well.

191
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:07,910
Thank you!

192
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:09,810
The latte...

193
00:15:10,943 --> 00:15:13,743
Still, I envy Seo Jun's mom sometimes.

194
00:15:13,743 --> 00:15:17,110
It's hard, but at least
she gets to keep working.

195
00:15:17,110 --> 00:15:21,076
I only planned to take a short break,
but sometimes I regret staying home.

196
00:15:21,076 --> 00:15:22,110
Me too.

197
00:15:22,110 --> 00:15:26,676
After spending all day dealing with my kid,
I sometimes miss working outside too.

198
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:28,843
Who wouldn't want to keep working?

199
00:15:28,843 --> 00:15:32,110
Is there anyone here
who doesn't want to work?

200
00:15:32,110 --> 00:15:34,543
That's why I call it being greedy.

201
00:15:34,543 --> 00:15:37,176
Kids need so much attention at that age.

202
00:15:37,176 --> 00:15:40,776
How can you leave them and work?

203
00:15:40,776 --> 00:15:42,943
Is it really impossible?

204
00:15:44,343 --> 00:15:46,943
Is it really that hard to work
while raising a child?

205
00:15:46,943 --> 00:15:49,476
I really hope not...

206
00:15:49,476 --> 00:15:51,443
Why?

207
00:15:51,443 --> 00:15:54,076
I'm going back to work starting tomorrow.

208
00:15:54,076 --> 00:15:55,076
Oh, my.

209
00:15:55,076 --> 00:16:01,410
My parental leave ends today,
so I'm going back to work tomorrow...

210
00:16:01,410 --> 00:16:04,643
Wait, you were a working mom this whole time?

211
00:16:04,643 --> 00:16:07,610
How did we not know?

212
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:11,643
What, so you were just
taking a break from work?

213
00:16:11,643 --> 00:16:13,210
How long were you off work?

214
00:16:13,210 --> 00:16:16,043
- One year?
- Three years.

215
00:16:16,776 --> 00:16:18,976
I wanted to wait until my child
was a little older before going back...

216
00:16:18,976 --> 00:16:20,776
Three years? Are you a civil servant?

217
00:16:20,776 --> 00:16:22,643
Or do you work for a major company?

218
00:16:22,643 --> 00:16:25,843
No, I just work for a small company.

219
00:16:26,510 --> 00:16:28,510
A small company.

220
00:16:28,510 --> 00:16:30,310
Small...

221
00:16:32,176 --> 00:16:37,676
I really enjoyed having
morning coffee together like this,

222
00:16:37,676 --> 00:16:40,876
and learning parenting tips from you all.

223
00:16:40,876 --> 00:16:43,576
And the coffee here is so delicious, right?

224
00:16:59,210 --> 00:17:01,643
<i>Today is D-Day. Soryong Nightclub, Musan.</i>

225
00:17:01,643 --> 00:17:06,310
Today? Why does it have to be today?

226
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:11,510
This won't do. This is a problem.

227
00:17:11,510 --> 00:17:13,843
I'm really in trouble now. Oh, my.

228
00:17:15,476 --> 00:17:18,976
Honey, I'm sorry. Really.
But this D-day was scheduled first...

229
00:17:18,976 --> 00:17:21,876
I'll really make it up to you.

230
00:17:28,743 --> 00:17:30,543
[Mother]

231
00:17:30,543 --> 00:17:33,063
Mother? Yes.

232
00:17:33,063 --> 00:17:35,847
Yeah, it's fine. Go ahead.

233
00:17:38,076 --> 00:17:39,810
It must be a great company.

234
00:17:39,810 --> 00:17:42,376
It's not easy to take the full three years
of parental leave.

235
00:17:42,376 --> 00:17:45,576
Or maybe she's just really capable?

236
00:17:45,576 --> 00:17:49,510
Well, she's been off for three years.
Why bother going back now...

237
00:17:51,643 --> 00:17:52,976
I got it!

238
00:17:52,976 --> 00:17:54,043
What is it?

239
00:17:54,043 --> 00:17:56,043
The husband must be
struggling financially, I guess.

240
00:17:56,043 --> 00:17:59,243
- Oh, no.
- That must have been hard.

241
00:17:59,243 --> 00:18:00,576
She never told us.

242
00:18:00,576 --> 00:18:03,910
Well, she has to earn her own money, I guess.

243
00:18:05,610 --> 00:18:09,210
<i>More than half of the drug cases
uncovered by police in recent months</i>

244
00:18:09,210 --> 00:18:12,843
<i>have involved people in their 20s and 30s.</i>

245
00:18:12,843 --> 00:18:16,810
<i>New types of drugs, including
liquid marijuana, ketamine, and fentanyl,</i>

246
00:18:16,810 --> 00:18:18,676
<i>are reportedly spreading</i>

247
00:18:18,676 --> 00:18:24,043
<i>among ordinary office workers and students
through clubs and private academies.</i>

248
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:32,110
Mother, I'm here! Hello, Sister-in-law.

249
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:34,910
Oh, my, you're here. What brings you here?

250
00:18:34,910 --> 00:18:37,176
I made some radish kimchi
that Tae Seong likes.

251
00:18:37,176 --> 00:18:39,443
Oh, radish kimchi?

252
00:18:40,810 --> 00:18:43,943
Let me get that, Mother. Just leave it.

253
00:18:43,943 --> 00:18:47,543
Wow, it looks so appetizing
just from the sight of it.

254
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:51,643
My mom sure has all kinds of excuses
to call her daughter-in-law over.

255
00:18:51,643 --> 00:18:54,143
Will my son even eat properly
starting tomorrow?

256
00:18:54,143 --> 00:18:57,010
Don't worry, Mother.
I'll make sure he eats well.

257
00:18:57,010 --> 00:18:59,276
No wonder you treat him
like your precious only son.

258
00:18:59,276 --> 00:19:01,476
I'm sure she'll take good care of him.

259
00:19:01,476 --> 00:19:05,410
These days, daughters-in-law don't really
like their mothers-in-law fussing over them.

260
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:06,610
Is that so?

261
00:19:06,610 --> 00:19:09,043
No, Mother. I really appreciate it.

262
00:19:09,043 --> 00:19:11,943
Thank you, Mother. We'll enjoy it.

263
00:19:11,943 --> 00:19:17,576
No matter how busy I was,
I've never fed my family instant food.

264
00:19:17,576 --> 00:19:19,376
I'll keep that in mind, Mother.

265
00:19:19,376 --> 00:19:25,471
Speaking of which, Mother,
that soy-marinated crab, jellyfish salad,

266
00:19:25,471 --> 00:19:26,471
and pickled perilla leaves
you made last time,

267
00:19:26,471 --> 00:19:28,710
could you make them again?

268
00:19:29,510 --> 00:19:31,643
- Huh?
- Tae Seong really loved them.

269
00:19:31,643 --> 00:19:33,276
We finished them in less than three days.

270
00:19:33,276 --> 00:19:35,510
Oh, sure, I'll make them.

271
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:37,710
Really? Thank you.

272
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:39,510
Is there anything
I can help you with, Mother?

273
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:43,510
Oh, no, just go quickly.
You probably have a lot to prepare.

274
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:44,676
- No, it's fine.
- Oh, my.

275
00:19:44,676 --> 00:19:48,143
Why does my shoulder hurt so much today?

276
00:19:48,143 --> 00:19:49,610
- When am I going to finish all this...
- Mother, leave it.

277
00:19:49,610 --> 00:19:52,110
- I'll do it. Leave it.
- Mother!

278
00:19:58,043 --> 00:20:00,310
Okay, let's do this.

279
00:20:09,376 --> 00:20:12,210
Oh, Mom, really...

280
00:20:12,210 --> 00:20:15,710
Do you really have to work her
on her last day off?

281
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:18,576
I'm not making her do anything.
She offered to do it.

282
00:20:18,576 --> 00:20:19,976
Oh, dear.

283
00:20:19,976 --> 00:20:22,243
- What?
- Oh, hello.

284
00:20:22,243 --> 00:20:24,110
Is your daughter-in-law
going back to work tomorrow?

285
00:20:24,110 --> 00:20:26,043
She's returning to work or something.

286
00:20:26,043 --> 00:20:28,610
Oh! That's good.

287
00:20:28,610 --> 00:20:32,176
It's hard to make a living on
one income these days.

288
00:20:32,176 --> 00:20:35,210
My son has been working himself
to the bone supporting the family alone.

289
00:20:35,210 --> 00:20:36,876
So, was she just sitting around
all this time?

290
00:20:36,876 --> 00:20:40,776
Jeez, I'm sure her salary
is barely anything anyway.

291
00:20:40,776 --> 00:20:42,210
She's already acting all high and mighty.

292
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:43,843
Mom!

293
00:20:43,843 --> 00:20:45,943
When did she ever act like that?

294
00:20:45,943 --> 00:20:50,110
Didn't you say your daughter-in-law
worked for some big company?

295
00:20:50,110 --> 00:20:52,143
Was it some place
that sells refrigerators and TVs?

296
00:20:52,143 --> 00:20:54,310
You're talking nonsense.

297
00:20:54,310 --> 00:20:57,643
That one. She works for that fan company.

298
00:21:00,376 --> 00:21:01,743
I need to replace my fan.

299
00:21:01,743 --> 00:21:04,310
Can you get an employee discount
or something?

300
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:06,543
They probably don't make much money
selling those anyway.

301
00:21:06,543 --> 00:21:08,743
Anyway, why are you here?

302
00:21:08,743 --> 00:21:09,976
- Did you hear?
- Hear what?

303
00:21:09,976 --> 00:21:14,410
That Chinese restaurant in the front
shopping area is closing down.

304
00:21:14,410 --> 00:21:17,876
What? Isn't that the place
where people line up to eat?

305
00:21:17,876 --> 00:21:19,143
Why are they suddenly closing?

306
00:21:19,143 --> 00:21:22,643
Apparently the building owner
tripled the rent.

307
00:21:22,643 --> 00:21:24,576
- Oh, my.
- What else could it mean?

308
00:21:24,576 --> 00:21:25,576
They're telling them to leave.

309
00:21:25,576 --> 00:21:27,710
Wow, that's really nasty.

310
00:21:27,710 --> 00:21:31,143
Since business is good, they want to
open their own restaurant there.

311
00:21:36,343 --> 00:21:39,143
[Tae Seong Chicken]

312
00:21:47,843 --> 00:21:49,191
[Big sale today:
30% off select industrial products]

313
00:21:49,191 --> 00:21:51,176
[50% off all agricultural products]
Oh, the mart is having a sale.

314
00:22:10,976 --> 00:22:13,610
At least I've been lucky with my landlord.

315
00:22:13,610 --> 00:22:16,076
The rent for all the shops around here
goes up every year,

316
00:22:16,076 --> 00:22:18,476
but mine has stayed the same for five years.

317
00:22:18,476 --> 00:22:20,210
It'll probably stay that way
this time too, right?

318
00:22:20,210 --> 00:22:21,210
I guess so.

319
00:22:21,210 --> 00:22:24,976
Oh! Oh, my gosh! You're being too naive.

320
00:22:24,976 --> 00:22:27,176
How can you be so sure
about someone's intentions?

321
00:22:27,176 --> 00:22:31,143
After five years frozen, they could raise it
all at once, and we'd have no say.

322
00:22:31,143 --> 00:22:33,443
Oh, no way!

323
00:22:33,443 --> 00:22:36,543
Business isn't even good these days.

324
00:22:47,710 --> 00:22:49,276
If you're really worried,

325
00:22:49,276 --> 00:22:52,810
you should visit the landlord beforehand
and show some appreciation.

326
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:55,643
Who could say no to a smiling face?

327
00:23:00,310 --> 00:23:03,476
Sun Il, let's go buy a gift right now.

328
00:23:03,476 --> 00:23:06,843
The landlord must be loaded.
What are you going to buy?

329
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:08,076
I guess you're right.

330
00:23:08,076 --> 00:23:09,843
What should we buy, then?

331
00:23:10,610 --> 00:23:11,976
Ask your daughter-in-law.

332
00:23:11,976 --> 00:23:15,476
Young moms usually
have a better sense for these things.

333
00:23:15,476 --> 00:23:17,910
What sense? My foot.

334
00:23:17,910 --> 00:23:21,843
She showed up empty-handed
the first time she came to meet

335
00:23:21,843 --> 00:23:23,210
her future mother-in-law.

336
00:23:23,210 --> 00:23:27,143
One time, I asked her to buy
some red ginseng as a gift,

337
00:23:27,143 --> 00:23:30,310
and she brought back
a whole fresh ginseng root instead.

338
00:23:30,310 --> 00:23:33,243
Come on, no way!

339
00:23:36,243 --> 00:23:38,843
My sister-in-law is just a little unusual.

340
00:23:38,843 --> 00:23:41,776
Sometimes she just doesn't know things
everyone else does.

341
00:23:41,776 --> 00:23:43,476
Really?

342
00:23:46,476 --> 00:23:48,310
Well, that's probably
because she's an orphan.

343
00:23:48,310 --> 00:23:51,943
She didn't have parents
to learn those things from.

344
00:23:51,943 --> 00:23:53,843
Bye.

345
00:23:54,810 --> 00:23:57,510
Oh, what do you mean help?

346
00:23:57,510 --> 00:24:00,943
She couldn't even stick around and ran off...

347
00:24:04,843 --> 00:24:08,143
When did she chop all of this?

348
00:24:08,143 --> 00:24:10,410
Look at how even they are.

349
00:24:10,410 --> 00:24:13,676
How can this...

350
00:24:13,676 --> 00:24:15,643
I'm scared.

351
00:24:15,643 --> 00:24:17,643
- What's this?
- What is going on?

352
00:24:17,643 --> 00:24:19,776
[Black Beans]

353
00:24:19,776 --> 00:24:20,876
Black beans...

354
00:24:20,876 --> 00:24:22,843
[Today Only: Unbeatable Price,
50% Off All Agricultural Products]

355
00:24:22,843 --> 00:24:25,576
- These onions are nice and big.
- They're so cheap.

356
00:24:25,576 --> 00:24:27,710
- The autumn squash is a good price.
- Oh, my.

357
00:24:27,710 --> 00:24:30,576
They're doing something over there too.
Let's go check it out.

358
00:24:38,410 --> 00:24:40,143
Miss Kim!

359
00:24:41,543 --> 00:24:43,643
What are you doing after work?

360
00:24:43,643 --> 00:24:45,510
I asked what you're doing afterward.

361
00:24:45,510 --> 00:24:47,143
Why are you acting like this?

362
00:24:47,143 --> 00:24:50,843
Come on, just stay a minute.
You like this, don't you?

363
00:24:50,843 --> 00:24:52,843
Please don't do this.

364
00:24:54,710 --> 00:24:56,576
I'll get going now.

365
00:25:01,943 --> 00:25:03,710
Who was that?

366
00:25:06,143 --> 00:25:08,010
Miss Kim!

367
00:25:14,843 --> 00:25:16,443
Oh, my back!

368
00:25:16,443 --> 00:25:18,176
[Trash Can Deodorizer]
Who did this?

369
00:25:18,176 --> 00:25:19,943
Who was it?

370
00:25:24,143 --> 00:25:25,743
Oh, my.

371
00:25:26,410 --> 00:25:28,510
<i>Now, for the next 30 minutes only,</i>

372
00:25:28,510 --> 00:25:30,643
<i>we're offering our seasonal
health-boosting samgyetang</i>

373
00:25:30,643 --> 00:25:34,043
<i>at a special buy-one-get-one deal.</i>

374
00:25:34,043 --> 00:25:36,243
Got the samgyetang!

375
00:25:46,576 --> 00:25:48,576
[Big Precious]

376
00:25:51,043 --> 00:25:55,276
Honey, I love you!
I'll really make it up to you.

377
00:26:05,976 --> 00:26:09,810
Wow, my wife really saw it coming.

378
00:26:09,810 --> 00:26:12,610
[Musan Soryong Nightclub]

379
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:15,243
Wait, get out. Get out.

380
00:26:15,243 --> 00:26:16,810
Come here. I need to wipe your feet.

381
00:26:16,810 --> 00:26:18,543
No, I don't want to!

382
00:26:18,543 --> 00:26:20,843
Yul, come here! You have to wipe your feet.

383
00:26:20,843 --> 00:26:22,743
You'll catch a cold. Hurry.

384
00:26:24,043 --> 00:26:26,976
Okay. Then stay right there.

385
00:26:37,043 --> 00:26:40,643
<i>Honey, I'm in Musan right now.</i>

386
00:26:40,643 --> 00:26:44,076
<i>Something urgent came up
for a business trip, so I might be late.</i>

387
00:26:44,910 --> 00:26:49,076
<i>I was supposed to get home early
and help you... I'm sorry.</i>

388
00:26:49,076 --> 00:26:51,376
<i>I'll take the last bus and come,
even if I'm late.</i>

389
00:26:51,376 --> 00:26:53,276
<i>I love you, Bo Na.</i>

390
00:26:53,276 --> 00:26:55,410
<i>You know how much I love you, right?</i>

391
00:26:55,410 --> 00:26:57,876
Oh, this man, seriously...

392
00:27:06,376 --> 00:27:09,076
Just wait until you get home.
You're not getting away with this.

393
00:27:09,076 --> 00:27:12,276
<i>It can't be helped. It's okay.</i>

394
00:27:12,276 --> 00:27:14,176
<i>Take care of your work and don't worry.</i>

395
00:27:14,176 --> 00:27:16,343
<i>Just stop sending those crying emojis.</i>

396
00:27:22,810 --> 00:27:24,610
Yul, let's get dressed now!

397
00:27:24,610 --> 00:27:25,910
- Come here.
- No, I don't want to.

398
00:27:25,910 --> 00:27:26,910
Come here!

399
00:27:26,910 --> 00:27:28,943
- Come on, hurry.
- No!

400
00:27:28,943 --> 00:27:30,043
Come quickly.

401
00:27:30,043 --> 00:27:32,910
Come here! Come here!

402
00:28:57,543 --> 00:28:59,110
Boss, I'll just go use
the bathroom real quick.

403
00:28:59,110 --> 00:29:00,110
You punk!

404
00:29:00,110 --> 00:29:01,876
I'm sorry.

405
00:29:01,876 --> 00:29:03,476
Give it to me!

406
00:29:24,676 --> 00:29:26,976
[Empty Taxi]
Follow that black car, please.

407
00:29:29,210 --> 00:29:30,810
Let's sleep.

408
00:29:30,810 --> 00:29:33,710
I'm going to sleep with Daddy.
When's Daddy coming?

409
00:29:33,710 --> 00:29:36,543
I told you that Daddy is busy with work
and will be late today.

410
00:29:36,543 --> 00:29:38,310
Sleep with me, okay?

411
00:29:38,310 --> 00:29:40,910
No, I'll sleep when Daddy gets home.

412
00:29:40,910 --> 00:29:43,576
Where did Daddy go?

413
00:29:43,576 --> 00:29:46,743
His work isn't finished yet.

414
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:49,143
Should I sing you a song?

415
00:29:49,143 --> 00:29:50,876
What kind of work?

416
00:29:52,610 --> 00:29:57,243
Daddy is doing...
something very, very important.

417
00:29:57,243 --> 00:30:02,810
He is a truly good man
who does wonderful things for people.

418
00:30:02,810 --> 00:30:04,776
A good person?

419
00:30:04,776 --> 00:30:10,943
Yes. A very good person
who makes the world brighter.

420
00:30:10,943 --> 00:30:11,976
Yeah, honey.

421
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:13,243
<i>Honey, are you on your way?</i>

422
00:30:13,243 --> 00:30:14,276
Yes, I'm on my way.

423
00:30:14,276 --> 00:30:16,810
<i>I prepared the barbecue,
but I haven't picked out the wine yet.</i>

424
00:30:16,810 --> 00:30:18,610
Barbecue with wine?

425
00:30:18,610 --> 00:30:21,043
Of course, Napa Cabernet.

426
00:30:21,043 --> 00:30:24,876
<i>Napa Cabernet? Okay, I'll get that, then.</i>

427
00:30:24,876 --> 00:30:26,843
<i>How much longer?</i>

428
00:30:35,943 --> 00:30:38,476
How far is he going?

429
00:30:45,743 --> 00:30:47,743
Sir, I'm almost out of time
for the last train.

430
00:30:47,743 --> 00:30:50,643
Is Musan Station far from here?
How long will it take?

431
00:30:50,643 --> 00:30:52,576
What, Musan Station?

432
00:31:07,376 --> 00:31:09,843
Oh, my, what happened here?

433
00:31:12,543 --> 00:31:14,043
Ambulance...

434
00:31:14,043 --> 00:31:16,710
- Call an ambulance. Now!
- Okay.

435
00:31:26,743 --> 00:31:31,376
Yes, hello. There's been
a vehicle explosion here.

436
00:31:38,476 --> 00:31:40,543
Rest in peace.

437
00:31:40,543 --> 00:31:43,776
I can't tell you to be reborn.

438
00:32:08,376 --> 00:32:12,176
Yul, we're late! Yul, get out!

439
00:32:12,876 --> 00:32:15,676
Yul, what did I say today was?

440
00:32:15,676 --> 00:32:17,910
- Your first day back at work!
- Right?

441
00:32:17,910 --> 00:32:21,210
Then who did I say would pick you up
after daycare today?

442
00:32:21,210 --> 00:32:22,276
Ms. Hee Seon!

443
00:32:22,276 --> 00:32:25,343
Yul, our Yul! Why are you so smart?

444
00:32:27,210 --> 00:32:29,143
Let's go, let's go. Hurry.

445
00:32:30,410 --> 00:32:32,043
Hello, Miss!

446
00:32:32,043 --> 00:32:35,276
Oh, my, Yul is a little late today.

447
00:32:35,276 --> 00:32:36,610
You're starting today, right?

448
00:32:36,610 --> 00:32:40,076
Yes, so starting today,
a helper will be picking Yul up.

449
00:32:40,076 --> 00:32:41,976
But it's our first time,
both for me and Yul, so...

450
00:32:41,976 --> 00:32:43,367
Oh, don't worry too much.

451
00:32:43,367 --> 00:32:44,843
I'll keep a close eye on Yul

452
00:32:44,843 --> 00:32:46,476
and contact you right away
if anything happens.

453
00:32:46,476 --> 00:32:48,076
Thank you.

454
00:32:48,076 --> 00:32:50,043
Yul. My Yul.

455
00:32:50,043 --> 00:32:51,510
- Today, too...
- Today, too, with friends...

456
00:32:51,510 --> 00:32:53,210
Get along well!

457
00:32:53,210 --> 00:32:54,676
See you later.

458
00:32:54,676 --> 00:32:56,010
Have a great day, Ma'am. Let's go in.

459
00:32:56,010 --> 00:32:57,910
Mommy, bye-bye!

460
00:33:01,610 --> 00:33:03,527
[Child on Board]

461
00:33:10,243 --> 00:33:12,543
Okay, let's get going.

462
00:33:16,276 --> 00:33:21,176
<i>Last night, a vehicle exploded on
an outer road in Musan while driving.</i>

463
00:33:21,176 --> 00:33:24,643
<i>The driver, a man in his 40s
identified as Mr. Bae, died at the scene.</i>

464
00:33:24,643 --> 00:33:27,110
<i>Police say they have asked the NFS
to analyze the crash vehicle</i>

465
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:32,910
<i>and perform an autopsy to determine
the details of the brutal case.</i>

466
00:33:32,910 --> 00:33:33,943
<i>In other news,</i>

467
00:33:33,943 --> 00:33:36,876
<i>Hwang, who had been serving time
for allegedly murdering his pregnant wife,</i>

468
00:33:36,876 --> 00:33:39,610
<i>has been released after three years,
sparking controversy.</i>

469
00:33:39,610 --> 00:33:42,776
<i>Three years ago, Hwang caused
an accident while driving drunk</i>

470
00:33:42,776 --> 00:33:47,643
<i>and was arrested for killing
his pregnant wife in the passenger seat.</i>

471
00:33:57,810 --> 00:33:59,543
What time is it now?

472
00:34:05,176 --> 00:34:08,543
<i>Honey, I missed the last train.</i>

473
00:34:08,543 --> 00:34:11,576
<i>I have some additional reporting to do,
so I think I need to stay here one more day.</i>

474
00:34:11,576 --> 00:34:13,976
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

475
00:34:13,976 --> 00:34:16,443
Just wait till you get home, Kwon Tae Seong.

476
00:34:25,243 --> 00:34:27,010
It's pretty.

477
00:34:28,276 --> 00:34:30,599
[Durumi Electronics]

478
00:34:36,210 --> 00:34:39,043
[Yoo Bo Na]

479
00:34:49,343 --> 00:34:51,975
[Durumi Electronics]

480
00:35:03,876 --> 00:35:05,243
Excuse me...

481
00:35:05,243 --> 00:35:07,743
What are you doing? Aren't you going in?

482
00:35:07,743 --> 00:35:11,376
Oh, this is so old.

483
00:35:11,376 --> 00:35:13,010
Excuse...

484
00:35:14,810 --> 00:35:16,679
I opened it temporarily for one day.

485
00:35:16,679 --> 00:35:18,910
You can get your new ID badge later.

486
00:35:18,910 --> 00:35:20,543
Pretty good.

487
00:35:28,543 --> 00:35:30,410
Ki Yeong Do, it's been a while.

488
00:35:30,410 --> 00:35:32,310
I'm Assistant Manager Ki.

489
00:35:32,310 --> 00:35:34,376
- What?
- It's been a while since I got promoted.

490
00:35:34,376 --> 00:35:38,743
You got promoted?
Congratulations, Assistant Manager Ki.

491
00:35:38,743 --> 00:35:39,943
You look great.

492
00:35:39,943 --> 00:35:41,776
You haven't changed a bit either.

493
00:35:41,776 --> 00:35:44,010
Really? I couldn't sleep last night.

494
00:35:44,010 --> 00:35:46,210
Why couldn't you sleep?

495
00:35:47,243 --> 00:35:49,743
- Because I heard you were coming back.
- Here it is.

496
00:35:50,910 --> 00:35:52,510
Let's go!

497
00:35:57,576 --> 00:36:00,276
Welcome back!

498
00:36:03,943 --> 00:36:05,543
[Welcome Back, Director Yoo Bo Na]

499
00:36:05,543 --> 00:36:07,010
You're finally back.

500
00:36:07,010 --> 00:36:10,476
Our Director Yoo Bo Na,
whom I've only heard about.

501
00:36:11,410 --> 00:36:13,176
Thank you.

502
00:36:15,343 --> 00:36:17,243
This is Assistant Manager Yang Ye Sol,
who joined while you were away.

503
00:36:17,243 --> 00:36:19,876
She took over from Jeong In Joo.

504
00:36:19,876 --> 00:36:21,676
I've heard so much about you.

505
00:36:21,676 --> 00:36:23,576
I heard you used to be the best on our team.

506
00:36:23,576 --> 00:36:27,043
I've seriously been waiting forever
to meet you.

507
00:36:27,043 --> 00:36:30,276
Not because of your performance or anything.

508
00:36:30,276 --> 00:36:33,843
Anyway, it's really great
to finally meet you.

509
00:36:33,843 --> 00:36:36,943
It's so good to meet you too.

510
00:36:39,743 --> 00:36:42,176
Manager Go, you've been
doing well too, right?

511
00:36:42,176 --> 00:36:43,910
Oh, yeah.

512
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:46,443
You're finally back, Director Yoo.

513
00:36:48,310 --> 00:36:50,476
I'll head to my desk.

514
00:37:04,210 --> 00:37:05,710
Is the team leader not here yet?

515
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:08,310
Oh, he went on a business trip
to Musan yesterday.

516
00:37:08,310 --> 00:37:10,510
He got back early this morning,
so he'll be a little late.

517
00:37:10,510 --> 00:37:12,410
Musan?

518
00:37:12,410 --> 00:37:14,543
Oh, I see.

519
00:37:16,510 --> 00:37:18,710
Is he still the same?

520
00:37:18,710 --> 00:37:20,610
Still the same.

521
00:37:20,610 --> 00:37:21,910
You're here?

522
00:37:21,910 --> 00:37:25,176
- You're here?
- Hi! Good morning!

523
00:37:25,176 --> 00:37:26,910
You swept the market again, huh?

524
00:37:26,910 --> 00:37:28,976
What is it this time, Team Leader?

525
00:37:31,310 --> 00:37:35,310
Lettuce. Look how fresh it is.

526
00:37:35,310 --> 00:37:37,076
Ms. Yoo Bo Na is here.

527
00:37:37,076 --> 00:37:38,710
What?

528
00:37:39,876 --> 00:37:41,676
Director Yoo!

529
00:37:47,243 --> 00:37:50,343
Wow, how long has it been?

530
00:37:50,343 --> 00:37:53,943
You're finally back! Our team's ace.

531
00:37:53,943 --> 00:37:56,710
Have you been well?

532
00:37:56,710 --> 00:37:59,176
You're still the same, Team Leader.

533
00:38:00,943 --> 00:38:06,410
Wow, with Director Yoo back,
the office feels full and lively.

534
00:38:06,410 --> 00:38:10,343
A person needs to have some presence.

535
00:38:11,143 --> 00:38:15,443
Oh, right. We'll catch up properly
when we have the time and money.

536
00:38:15,443 --> 00:38:19,876
But today, I have something
urgent on my mind.

537
00:38:21,476 --> 00:38:23,343
Welcome back.

538
00:38:25,276 --> 00:38:27,676
Alright, get back to work!

539
00:38:30,710 --> 00:38:34,076
[Musan City Police Station]

540
00:38:34,887 --> 00:38:35,975
[A Safe, Clean Sea of Hope]

541
00:38:50,276 --> 00:38:53,143
Excuse me, excuse me!

542
00:38:53,143 --> 00:38:55,810
I heard you were at the scene.
May I have your name?

543
00:38:55,810 --> 00:38:58,510
Oh, yes. Just a moment.

544
00:39:00,043 --> 00:39:03,276
I'm Kwon Tae Seong, a reporter
from Digging Deep News, Not Today.

545
00:39:03,276 --> 00:39:04,743
[Not Today Reporter, Kwon Tae Seong]
What's your name, sir?

546
00:39:04,743 --> 00:39:09,343
Well, what brings an investigative reporter
all the way from Seoul to Musan?

547
00:39:09,343 --> 00:39:11,143
Has the victim's identity been confirmed yet?

548
00:39:11,143 --> 00:39:14,176
What on earth is going on here?

549
00:39:14,176 --> 00:39:16,110
I think that's something
I should be asking you.

550
00:39:16,110 --> 00:39:18,310
So what exactly happened here?

551
00:39:18,310 --> 00:39:19,443
Excuse me?

552
00:39:19,443 --> 00:39:21,510
Well, the taxi driver said

553
00:39:21,510 --> 00:39:25,076
you came out of a club
and suddenly asked him to follow this car.

554
00:39:25,076 --> 00:39:26,710
So, what was that about?

555
00:39:26,710 --> 00:39:29,610
Well, what else would a reporter be doing?
I was covering a story.

556
00:39:29,610 --> 00:39:30,610
Like I am now.

557
00:39:30,610 --> 00:39:33,276
A story? What kind of story?

558
00:39:35,476 --> 00:39:39,076
We received information that a new type
of drug had infiltrated clubs around Musan.

559
00:39:39,076 --> 00:39:41,876
So I was meeting an informant today
for an interview, when...

560
00:39:41,876 --> 00:39:44,576
Oh, then what about the car?

561
00:39:44,576 --> 00:39:46,643
Why did you follow it?

562
00:39:48,843 --> 00:39:51,810
Am I a witness? A person of interest?

563
00:39:52,443 --> 00:39:53,876
Or am I a suspect?

564
00:39:53,876 --> 00:39:57,110
No, it's not like that.
Just tell me what happened...

565
00:39:57,110 --> 00:39:59,310
The informant said that man was a dropper.

566
00:39:59,310 --> 00:40:01,276
- A dropper?
- I was following him

567
00:40:01,276 --> 00:40:05,443
in case I could catch him
distributing drugs to other clubs.

568
00:40:05,443 --> 00:40:07,143
Drug-related reports

569
00:40:07,143 --> 00:40:11,476
tend to focus sensationally
on ordinary users consuming drugs.

570
00:40:11,476 --> 00:40:14,776
But I wanted to focus on the suppliers

571
00:40:14,776 --> 00:40:16,876
and expose how these drugs are distributed.

572
00:40:16,876 --> 00:40:18,876
I thought it could raise public awareness

573
00:40:18,876 --> 00:40:23,610
and also help your investigations
and arrests in making society safer.

574
00:40:23,610 --> 00:40:25,243
Does that answer your question?

575
00:40:26,310 --> 00:40:28,876
Oh, yeah. That's admirable.

576
00:40:28,876 --> 00:40:33,010
But if he's a dropper, isn't he just
a low-level errand boy who delivers drugs?

577
00:40:33,010 --> 00:40:37,176
Oh, dear, Mr. Reporter,
I guess you've got the wrong idea.

578
00:40:37,176 --> 00:40:39,643
- Pardon?
- For now, go home.

579
00:40:39,643 --> 00:40:41,031
We may contact you later
for a witness interview,

580
00:40:41,031 --> 00:40:43,576
so please be aware of that.

581
00:40:43,576 --> 00:40:46,376
As you can see,
the scene is a mess right now. I'm off.

582
00:40:46,376 --> 00:40:50,243
Please make sure you take
thorough photos of the scene.

583
00:40:52,210 --> 00:40:54,043
[Son Seok Gu]

584
00:41:00,376 --> 00:41:01,376
- Hello...
- <i>Why do you keep calling?</i>

585
00:41:01,376 --> 00:41:02,510
You're putting me in a difficult position.

586
00:41:02,510 --> 00:41:05,143
I've called you several times.
Why haven't you answered?

587
00:41:05,143 --> 00:41:08,710
I need to see you right now. Where are you?

588
00:41:08,710 --> 00:41:12,010
Meet? What for? It's chaos here
because of what happened.

589
00:41:12,010 --> 00:41:14,043
Don't contact me again.
I'm changing my number.

590
00:41:14,043 --> 00:41:17,110
Wait, hold on! Let me ask you just one thing.

591
00:41:17,110 --> 00:41:20,343
What happened to that dropper from yesterday?

592
00:41:20,343 --> 00:41:23,043
<i>Why are you asking about him?</i>

593
00:41:23,043 --> 00:41:26,810
He came back shortly
after you left yesterday.

594
00:41:26,810 --> 00:41:28,143
- Well, then...
- <i>I'm hanging up.</i>

595
00:41:28,143 --> 00:41:29,743
Hello...

596
00:41:44,810 --> 00:41:46,810
That persistent guy actually showed up.

597
00:41:46,810 --> 00:41:50,343
I told you over the phone
several times that it's not possible.

598
00:41:50,343 --> 00:41:52,010
Who was the victim in last night's incident?

599
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:54,910
Jeez, what kind of reporter is so pushy...

600
00:41:58,610 --> 00:42:01,743
I'm the one who witnessed
the scene firsthand. Look at me.

601
00:42:01,743 --> 00:42:03,143
I still feel sick to my stomach.

602
00:42:03,143 --> 00:42:07,476
Well, if you feel sick, you can go to
a pharmacy and get some medicine.

603
00:42:07,476 --> 00:42:09,076
I even betrayed my wife.

604
00:42:09,076 --> 00:42:13,510
I was supposed to get home
no matter what yesterday.

605
00:42:13,510 --> 00:42:15,876
Then hurry home now.

606
00:42:15,876 --> 00:42:18,076
Come on, it's already too late.

607
00:42:18,076 --> 00:42:21,643
Today was my wife's first day back at work.

608
00:42:21,643 --> 00:42:23,710
Sir, are you married? My daughter is four.

609
00:42:23,710 --> 00:42:27,676
Why are you telling me
your daughter is four right now?

610
00:42:27,676 --> 00:42:29,843
I mean, it's not really relevant...

611
00:42:29,843 --> 00:42:32,643
Anyway, the victim, Mr. Bae,
is the drug kingpin Bae Doo Hyuk, right?

612
00:42:32,643 --> 00:42:35,376
Well, that's true, but...

613
00:42:37,110 --> 00:42:39,410
Come on.

614
00:42:39,410 --> 00:42:43,495
Was this just an accident?
Or... was it possibly murder?

615
00:42:46,439 --> 00:42:47,576
Come out.

616
00:42:47,576 --> 00:42:48,843
- Is that right?
- Come out!

617
00:42:48,843 --> 00:42:49,910
Please just tell me once.

618
00:42:49,910 --> 00:42:52,043
I said come out. Come out.

619
00:42:52,043 --> 00:42:54,976
- Well, Director Yoo.
- Yes?

620
00:42:54,976 --> 00:42:57,610
I feel bad asking this
on your first day back,

621
00:42:57,610 --> 00:43:02,010
but today, could you do a client meeting?

622
00:43:03,710 --> 00:43:04,976
Today, right away?

623
00:43:04,976 --> 00:43:06,443
Yeah, today.

624
00:43:06,443 --> 00:43:08,243
I know it's a lot to ask on your first day.

625
00:43:08,243 --> 00:43:11,276
And I know you're not someone
who does things halfway.

626
00:43:11,276 --> 00:43:15,510
But the client said today is
the only time they can make it.

627
00:43:15,510 --> 00:43:18,576
Assistant Manager Ki prepared everything.

628
00:43:20,276 --> 00:43:24,343
You just need to handle the meeting.

629
00:43:24,343 --> 00:43:25,543
[Client Report]

630
00:43:40,176 --> 00:43:41,676
You prepared everything thoroughly.

631
00:43:41,676 --> 00:43:43,776
I learned well from you.

632
00:43:47,176 --> 00:43:49,043
Let's do it during the day.

633
00:43:50,176 --> 00:43:51,510
During the day? Why?

634
00:43:51,510 --> 00:43:54,676
Considering the meeting location
and the client's schedule,

635
00:43:54,676 --> 00:43:56,376
having thought about it in detail,

636
00:43:56,376 --> 00:44:00,476
do you think it's strategically better
to do it during the day, Director Yoo?

637
00:44:00,476 --> 00:44:02,876
I have to pick up my kid.

638
00:44:04,843 --> 00:44:07,043
My husband is going to be late today.

639
00:44:10,643 --> 00:44:13,510
Let's do it during the day.

640
00:44:16,910 --> 00:44:19,815
[Client Information]

641
00:44:25,710 --> 00:44:30,343
Whether it's an accident or murder,
we'll know after the NFS results come out.

642
00:44:30,343 --> 00:44:34,110
And I wasn't the one who told you
the victim's name, okay?

643
00:44:41,863 --> 00:44:43,676
[A Safe, Clean Sea of Hope]

644
00:44:43,676 --> 00:44:46,210
Please take me to
the Musan Forensic Science Institute.

645
00:45:11,910 --> 00:45:14,376
I like the meeting venue.

646
00:45:15,610 --> 00:45:18,343
<i>The client arrived an hour ago
and is waiting inside.</i>

647
00:45:18,343 --> 00:45:19,343
<i>You can go right in.</i>

648
00:45:19,343 --> 00:45:21,710
Okay, let's see what you've got.

649
00:45:21,710 --> 00:45:23,710
Me?

650
00:45:23,710 --> 00:45:24,976
Oh, come on. Of course, I...

651
00:45:24,976 --> 00:45:27,110
Not you, me.

652
00:45:28,110 --> 00:45:30,176
Are you nervous?

653
00:45:30,176 --> 00:45:33,043
<i>Well, I guess it has been a while.</i>

654
00:45:33,043 --> 00:45:34,810
That's true for you.

655
00:45:34,810 --> 00:45:36,810
Stop shaking your leg.

656
00:45:50,510 --> 00:45:53,276
You too, Team Leader. Relax your grip.

657
00:46:14,183 --> 00:46:15,243
[Please Hear Our Prayer]

658
00:46:15,243 --> 00:46:17,076
Have you ever prayed?

659
00:46:17,076 --> 00:46:19,343
Of course not. What about you?

660
00:46:19,343 --> 00:46:23,143
Sometimes, without realizing it,
during moments that really shake me.

661
00:46:25,310 --> 00:46:28,843
You have moments like that too? When?

662
00:46:28,843 --> 00:46:33,110
When the child is chewing on
something and eating.

663
00:46:53,210 --> 00:46:55,343
<i>Isn't it a good thing if the child eats well?</i>

664
00:46:55,343 --> 00:46:57,810
The problem is that I never gave
the child anything to eat.

665
00:46:57,810 --> 00:47:00,376
Nothing has ever scared me
more than that moment.

666
00:47:09,810 --> 00:47:13,010
<i>You should see a long bench
in the right corner.</i>

667
00:47:13,010 --> 00:47:14,643
Yeah, I see it.

668
00:47:16,876 --> 00:47:21,210
Do you know when it's hardest
to comfort a crying four-year-old?

669
00:47:21,210 --> 00:47:24,276
- <i>When?</i>
- When a friend gets hurt at daycare.

670
00:47:24,276 --> 00:47:26,610
Oh, out of sadness?

671
00:47:26,610 --> 00:47:31,476
No, guilt. She thought
it was her fault and cried for an hour.

672
00:47:31,476 --> 00:47:33,943
Come on, what does a four-year-old even know?

673
00:47:33,943 --> 00:47:36,176
They know. Even four-year-olds.

674
00:47:36,176 --> 00:47:37,210
What?

675
00:47:37,210 --> 00:47:41,943
They know that they shouldn't
hurt someone, even by accident.

676
00:47:43,910 --> 00:47:45,843
Okay, shall we go?

677
00:47:48,410 --> 00:47:50,310
Now is a good time.

678
00:48:32,376 --> 00:48:36,876
Sales Team 3, Yoo Bo Na,
starting client meeting.

679
00:49:28,076 --> 00:49:29,943
Meeting concluded.

680
00:49:50,010 --> 00:49:52,176
Still got it.

681
00:50:07,543 --> 00:50:09,676
Rest in peace.

682
00:50:11,243 --> 00:50:14,376
I can't tell you to be reborn.

683
00:50:34,543 --> 00:50:37,210
Yoo Bo Na comes back.

684
00:50:59,010 --> 00:51:02,243
- Yul.
- Mommy!

685
00:51:02,243 --> 00:51:03,843
Yul!

686
00:51:03,843 --> 00:51:06,043
- Chae Won, hello.
- Hello.

687
00:51:06,043 --> 00:51:08,610
Did you have fun playing with Chae Won today?

688
00:51:08,610 --> 00:51:11,076
Yeah, I made this with her.

689
00:51:11,076 --> 00:51:12,110
Mommy, it's a present for you!

690
00:51:12,110 --> 00:51:14,843
What is this? Is it a rose?

691
00:51:14,843 --> 00:51:15,943
Yeah.

692
00:51:15,943 --> 00:51:17,476
But it's not my birthday today.

693
00:51:17,476 --> 00:51:20,743
I told her you had a hard first day
back at work, and she made this.

694
00:51:20,743 --> 00:51:23,376
Oh, you did that, Yul?

695
00:51:23,376 --> 00:51:24,876
You like flowers.

696
00:51:24,876 --> 00:51:26,976
Yes, that's right! You're the best, Yul.

697
00:51:26,976 --> 00:51:29,410
My Yul is the best! Thank you.

698
00:51:29,410 --> 00:51:32,043
Let me see, Yul. It looks just like you.

699
00:51:32,043 --> 00:51:34,876
Oh, you're so cute.

700
00:51:34,876 --> 00:51:36,676
Thank you!

701
00:51:37,310 --> 00:51:39,343
Let's go home now, okay?

702
00:51:50,610 --> 00:51:53,110
What concept is this supposed to be?

703
00:51:53,110 --> 00:51:56,076
It's the kind of face you talk about
when you say someone has no shame.

704
00:51:56,076 --> 00:51:58,943
It's not funny at all. Stop it.

705
00:52:03,976 --> 00:52:05,810
Honey, I'm sorry...

706
00:52:05,810 --> 00:52:09,343
I'll go without soup for a month.
I think I can handle it.

707
00:52:09,343 --> 00:52:11,010
Will that be enough?

708
00:52:11,010 --> 00:52:13,043
Not enough?

709
00:52:13,043 --> 00:52:14,976
I'm really sorry.

710
00:52:15,676 --> 00:52:17,543
What exactly are you sorry for?

711
00:52:18,876 --> 00:52:22,776
I mean, I really was going to come home,
even if it was late, but...

712
00:52:22,776 --> 00:52:24,710
Oh, is that all you have to say?

713
00:52:28,243 --> 00:52:30,176
I was going to come home
no matter how late it was.

714
00:52:30,176 --> 00:52:33,410
I even booked the last train ticket.

715
00:52:33,410 --> 00:52:35,743
How could you do this to me?

716
00:52:35,743 --> 00:52:36,943
That's how reporting is, you know.

717
00:52:36,943 --> 00:52:38,023
Once a story breaks,

718
00:52:38,023 --> 00:52:41,143
one thing leads to another,
and it just keeps snowballing...

719
00:52:41,143 --> 00:52:43,476
How could you only buy something for Yul?

720
00:52:43,476 --> 00:52:45,076
What?

721
00:52:47,943 --> 00:52:53,210
Yul, you can only have two. No more, okay?

722
00:52:54,876 --> 00:52:58,643
How could you only buy
the cream-flavored walnut cakes?

723
00:53:00,310 --> 00:53:02,976
You like red bean filling, right?

724
00:53:02,976 --> 00:53:04,476
I really do.

725
00:53:04,476 --> 00:53:07,043
Ever since we first met
about seven years ago,

726
00:53:07,043 --> 00:53:11,143
I think I've only eaten red bean bread,
red bean porridge, and red bean noodles...

727
00:53:11,143 --> 00:53:13,676
Did you already forget that?

728
00:53:13,676 --> 00:53:15,210
I remember.

729
00:53:15,210 --> 00:53:17,510
But how could you...

730
00:53:17,510 --> 00:53:22,343
Yul, put that down.
No, you can't have more than two.

731
00:53:22,343 --> 00:53:23,543
Eat it after dinner.

732
00:53:23,543 --> 00:53:25,210
Okay.

733
00:53:26,076 --> 00:53:28,943
But how could you...

734
00:53:28,943 --> 00:53:32,276
This is the mouth that has no excuses.

735
00:53:33,043 --> 00:53:34,810
- You laughed!
- No, I didn't.

736
00:53:34,810 --> 00:53:36,276
Huh? You laughed.

737
00:53:36,276 --> 00:53:38,010
You laughed! It's over when you smile.

738
00:53:38,010 --> 00:53:40,276
Yul, Mommy laughed!

739
00:53:42,376 --> 00:53:44,676
I'm letting it slide because of Yul, okay?

740
00:53:44,676 --> 00:53:47,510
I'm letting it go because Yul
helped make things easier for me.

741
00:53:47,510 --> 00:53:49,243
Yeah.

742
00:53:54,976 --> 00:53:58,710
Yul did that? Did you help Mommy
even for Daddy's sake?

743
00:53:58,710 --> 00:54:01,410
Oh, my, so cute!

744
00:54:01,410 --> 00:54:04,310
No, wash your hands before touching her.
Yul already took a bath.

745
00:54:04,310 --> 00:54:06,543
I won't touch her. I'll just hug her.

746
00:54:06,543 --> 00:54:09,110
You're my precious treasure.

747
00:54:09,110 --> 00:54:11,276
Right, how was your first day back at work?

748
00:54:11,276 --> 00:54:12,276
After such a long time...

749
00:54:12,276 --> 00:54:14,210
Yul, let's eat after dinner.

750
00:54:14,210 --> 00:54:16,676
- You'll get scolded by Mommy.
- Well, everyone helped me out.

751
00:54:16,676 --> 00:54:19,576
Still, it's something I've done for
a long time, so it came back quickly.

752
00:54:19,576 --> 00:54:22,243
I knew you'd do great. I told you, right?

753
00:54:22,243 --> 00:54:24,443
You'd get back into
the swing of things quickly.

754
00:54:26,343 --> 00:54:29,810
Honey, go wash up quickly. We need to eat.

755
00:54:29,810 --> 00:54:32,776
No, you're tired.
Let's just make do with this today.

756
00:54:32,776 --> 00:54:35,910
Sure, if you say so.
But it's still samgyetang.

757
00:54:35,910 --> 00:54:37,810
Samgyetang?

758
00:54:39,010 --> 00:54:40,676
Yul, she says it's samgyetang.

759
00:54:40,676 --> 00:54:42,910
I will go wash up quickly, okay?

760
00:54:50,910 --> 00:54:52,810
<i>The tenant from Tae Seong Chicken
on the first floor</i>

761
00:54:52,810 --> 00:54:57,110
<i>wanted to visit and greet you in person,
but I declined on your behalf.</i>

762
00:54:57,110 --> 00:55:01,610
<i>But they want to send you a gift.
What should I do?</i>

763
00:55:07,176 --> 00:55:08,910
Honey, can you get me a towel?

764
00:55:08,910 --> 00:55:10,876
Yeah, hold on!

765
00:55:12,176 --> 00:55:13,943
<i>Please politely decline.</i>

766
00:55:13,943 --> 00:55:16,943
<i>And I'll also freeze the rent for next month.</i>

767
00:55:16,943 --> 00:55:18,976
- Thank you for the meal!
- Eat plenty.

768
00:55:18,976 --> 00:55:20,743
Yul, try this.

769
00:55:21,743 --> 00:55:23,076
- Is it good?
- Yeah.

770
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:24,487
It's super, super good!

771
00:55:24,487 --> 00:55:26,643
Super, super good?

772
00:55:26,643 --> 00:55:28,910
But Yul, didn't you miss Daddy?

773
00:55:28,910 --> 00:55:30,476
- I missed you!
- How much?

774
00:55:30,476 --> 00:55:31,910
This much!

775
00:55:31,910 --> 00:55:34,143
You missed him this much?

776
00:55:34,143 --> 00:55:36,643
Dance as much as you enjoy the food!

777
00:55:54,183 --> 00:55:58,727
[Ok's Flower Shop]

778
00:56:05,443 --> 00:56:08,476
You're early! Did you change your schedule?

779
00:56:08,476 --> 00:56:10,643
Well, right. You have to go to work now.

780
00:56:10,643 --> 00:56:13,743
Why did you open so early?
The sun isn't even up yet.

781
00:56:13,743 --> 00:56:18,110
I need to catch customers on their way
to work. Making a living is tough.

782
00:56:18,110 --> 00:56:21,910
I thought you'd finally have some free time
after sending your kid to daycare.

783
00:56:21,910 --> 00:56:24,043
How does it feel to be back?

784
00:56:25,210 --> 00:56:26,676
My life is about to get a lot busier.

785
00:56:26,676 --> 00:56:29,743
And the world will get noisier, huh?

786
00:56:32,610 --> 00:56:34,276
What flower is this? Is it cosmos?

787
00:56:34,276 --> 00:56:35,276
It's a marguerite.

788
00:56:35,276 --> 00:56:36,310
Oh, marguerite.

789
00:56:36,310 --> 00:56:40,043
Its flower meanings are
"revealing secrets" and "true love."

790
00:56:40,043 --> 00:56:43,810
Come to think of it, this one flower
contains both "secret" and "truth."

791
00:56:43,810 --> 00:56:46,176
"A truthful person has no secrets."

792
00:56:46,176 --> 00:56:49,276
"True love means revealing your secrets."
Is that what it means?

793
00:56:49,276 --> 00:56:52,143
Well, I don't really like that meaning.

794
00:56:52,143 --> 00:56:55,243
Sometimes you keep secrets
because you love someone too much.

795
00:56:58,043 --> 00:57:00,643
Aren't you worried that

796
00:57:00,643 --> 00:57:03,976
the day might come
when your husband finds out?

797
00:57:09,143 --> 00:57:11,876
Well, the night before I went back to work,

798
00:57:11,876 --> 00:57:14,196
my husband promised he'd come home early,

799
00:57:14,196 --> 00:57:16,676
but then he suddenly had to go out of town.

800
00:57:16,676 --> 00:57:19,743
He said he'd come home
even if it was late, but he never did.

801
00:57:19,743 --> 00:57:20,776
Oh, dear.

802
00:57:20,776 --> 00:57:24,110
I knew it was because of his reporting,
but I was still hurt.

803
00:57:24,110 --> 00:57:27,310
I was busy getting ready,
but I just got upset for no reason.

804
00:57:27,310 --> 00:57:30,407
"Kwon Tae Seong, just you wait
till you get home tonight."

805
00:57:30,407 --> 00:57:35,010
There I was, all fired up by myself,
and then I just ended up laughing.

806
00:57:35,843 --> 00:57:38,676
I found myself so strange and amazing.

807
00:57:38,676 --> 00:57:41,676
And I still can't believe moments like that.

808
00:57:42,843 --> 00:57:44,476
I love them.

809
00:57:46,743 --> 00:57:48,976
So I'm not worried.

810
00:57:49,710 --> 00:57:52,043
Because that day will never come.

811
00:58:04,610 --> 00:58:07,776
<i>He's someone who lives in the light.</i>

812
00:58:07,776 --> 00:58:10,643
<i>Because he's different from me.</i>

813
00:58:10,643 --> 00:58:14,176
<i>Because if he knew how different we are,
we couldn't stay together.</i>

814
00:58:14,176 --> 00:58:16,976
You don't really know much about me, do you?

815
00:58:16,976 --> 00:58:19,043
I don't know much about you, Bo Na.

816
00:58:20,176 --> 00:58:22,310
I know your name, but...

817
00:58:23,410 --> 00:58:25,576
I don't even know if it's your real name.

818
00:58:27,176 --> 00:58:30,343
<i>Where you were born, how you grew up...</i>

819
00:58:42,743 --> 00:58:47,510
<i>What your family is like,
or what you do for a living...</i>

820
00:58:52,810 --> 00:58:54,215
<i>Why you were standing there</i>

821
00:58:54,215 --> 00:58:57,110
- <i>on the day we first met?</i>
- Hold on!

822
00:58:57,110 --> 00:58:59,510
- Come down, now!
- <i>I don't know those things either.</i>

823
00:58:59,510 --> 00:59:01,143
Oh, slowly!

824
00:59:01,143 --> 00:59:05,110
But I do know some aspects of you, Bo Na.

825
00:59:05,110 --> 00:59:07,410
Perhaps love begins...

826
00:59:08,410 --> 00:59:10,510
when you find yourself drawn to

827
00:59:10,510 --> 00:59:14,010
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

828
00:59:16,976 --> 00:59:19,476
I've already fallen in love.

829
00:59:26,343 --> 00:59:29,210
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

830
00:59:31,310 --> 00:59:35,743
Please take care of me.
It's my first time with love.

831
00:59:38,176 --> 00:59:41,776
<i>I'm not worried.
Because that day will never come.</i>

832
00:59:41,776 --> 00:59:47,010
<i>Because the day he sees
my other side will never come.</i>

833
00:59:50,343 --> 00:59:51,343
<i>Breaking news.</i>

834
00:59:51,343 --> 00:59:56,476
<i>A shooting using a sniper rifle
has occurred in the heart of Seoul.</i>

835
00:59:56,476 --> 01:00:01,010
<i>Some speculate that Kingfisher,
the infamous serial gun killer</i>

836
01:00:01,010 --> 01:00:03,510
[Breaking News: Kingfisher Returns?]
<i>who disappeared for the past four years,</i>

837
01:00:03,510 --> 01:00:05,810
[Shooting Homicide in Seoul]
<i>may have returned.</i>

838
01:00:05,810 --> 01:00:09,276
<i>The incident took place at a hotel
in Jeonjak-dong, Seoul.</i>

839
01:00:09,276 --> 01:00:11,276
<i>A man in his thirties,
identified as Mr. Hwang,</i>

840
01:00:11,276 --> 01:00:15,876
<i>was struck and killed by a bullet
fired from outside the building.</i>

841
01:00:15,876 --> 01:00:19,210
<i>For more details, we'll soon connect live to
our reporter on the scene</i>

842
01:00:19,210 --> 01:00:21,576
<i>for the latest on the police investigation...</i>

843
01:01:15,310 --> 01:01:17,143
A gun murder in South Korea?

844
01:01:17,143 --> 01:01:18,743
I think that punk is back.

845
01:01:18,743 --> 01:01:20,810
From now on, you're going
after Kingfisher, right?

846
01:01:20,810 --> 01:01:22,176
I'll really give it my all this time.

847
01:01:22,176 --> 01:01:23,176
Is it really the Kingfisher?

848
01:01:23,176 --> 01:01:24,775
[Musan Drug Kingpin's Car Explosion]
You're covering the Kingfisher story, right?

849
01:01:24,775 --> 01:01:26,310
Like, you find anything at the shooting site.

850
01:01:26,310 --> 01:01:27,376
Did you come here knowing something?

851
01:01:27,376 --> 01:01:29,776
Hey, you never know.
What if that was the real clue?

852
01:01:29,776 --> 01:01:30,823
[I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]
But sometimes,

853
01:01:30,823 --> 01:01:33,110
[Security Alert]
I think that day might actually come.

854
01:01:33,110 --> 01:01:35,110
He might find me.

855
01:01:35,110 --> 01:01:36,276
Shall I schedule a meeting?

856
01:01:36,276 --> 01:01:37,476
Don't you think something's strange?

857
01:01:37,476 --> 01:01:39,015
[Yoo Bo Na, Husband, Company]
Honestly, a guy like him

858
01:01:39,015 --> 01:01:40,775
getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

859
01:01:40,775 --> 01:01:44,976
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

860
01:01:47,543 --> 01:01:49,576
Where's Kwon Tae Seong?

